From: eirikr <151315375+Oichkatzelesfrettschen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 11:40:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] pl011: model the transmit FIFO level and raise the
 transmit interrupt on its crossing

The model reported TXFE always set, left TXFF and BUSY untagged, set the
Transmit raw status at UARTEN, at reset and when FEN cleared, and set it
again on every DATA write without ever clearing it, so an unmasked transmit
interrupt always fired. RP2040 datasheet 4.2.6.3 states that the interrupt
is based on a transition through a level: with FIFOs enabled it asserts
when the level falls to or below the TXIFLSEL trigger, clears when writes
raise the level above the trigger or ICR clears it, and stays clear when the
UART and the interrupt are enabled before any data is written; with FIFOs
disabled it asserts when the single location empties and clears on a write.

DATA still reaches the backend at write time. A level counter of 32
entries (one with FEN clear) stands for the characters the line has yet to
shift out and loses one entry per character time, scheduled by a
clock-source timer at the programmed divisors. TXFE reads level 0, TXFF
level full and BUSY level non-zero. TXIFLSEL is stored, defaults to 0b010
and selects 4, 8, 16, 24 or 28 entries; the trigger point is 0 with FIFOs
disabled. A write to a full FIFO is reported and discarded before it
reaches the backend, as on silicon: it changes neither the level nor the
raw status.
